llama.cpp (as fetched by Ollama v0.35.1, llama.cpp b11232, applied after
140): the HIP part of patch 140. The quantized matrix-vector kernels of
MUL_MAT_ID write zero rows for an expert id of -1 and read no weights for
it.

WHY
---
Patch 140 runs a token's hot experts on the GPU and its other experts on
the CPU, and passes each side the ids it should not compute as -1. Without
this patch mul_mat_vec_q would take -1 as an expert index and read memory
before the weights; with it, a block whose expert is -1 writes its rows as
zeros, which the sum with the CPU's output needs, and returns.
mul_mat_vec_q_moe (2-8 tokens with ids) gets the same check; patch 140
uses only one-token batches.

VERIFIED ON REAL HARDWARE: see patch 140 (the exactness runs go through
these kernels).
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu
